15 0 obj
<< /A 38 0 R /Alt (Risk of bias summary table with eight studies \(S1 to S8\) and five domains \(D1 to D5\). All domains except D4 show yellow ovals for \215Some concerns\216; D4 shows green ovals for \215Low risk.\216 Overall risk for all studies is red ovals for \215High risk.\216 Legend defines symbol colors and domain meanings.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 30 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 39 0 R /Alt (Horizontal bar chart displaying five categories of study bias. Four categories show all studies as having \215some concerns\216 in yellow. \215Bias in measurement of the outcome\216 is marked as \215low risk\216 in green. No categories display \215high risk\216 in red. Legend denotes green as low risk, yellow as some concerns, and red as high risk. X-axis represents percentage of studies from zero to one hundred percent.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 30 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 40 0 R /Alt (PRISMA flow diagram showing the identification and screening process for new studies via databases: 420 records identified, 143 duplicates removed, 277 screened, 224 excluded, 53 sought for retrieval, 6 not retrieved, 47 assessed, 39 excluded for eligibility reasons, and 8 studies included in review.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 31 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 41 0 R /Alt (Forest plot comparing GQD plus metformin versus metformin alone in two studies, showing individual and pooled mean differences with confidence intervals, overall mean difference of negative 1.92, substantial heterogeneity, and overall effect not statistically significant.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 33 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 42 0 R /Alt (\215Forest plot comparing two studies, S1 and S3, of GQD plus metformin versus metformin alone for HbA1c change scores using a correlation coefficient of r = 0.25. Individual and pooled mean differences with confidence intervals are shown. S1 shows a mean difference of approximately -3.20 and S3 shows approximately -0.64. The pooled mean difference is -1.92 with a 95% confidence interval of -4.43 to 0.59, indicating no statistically significant effect. Heterogeneity is high, with I-squared equal to 100 percent.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 33 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 43 0 R /Alt (Forest plot comparing two studies, S1 and S3, of GQD plus metformin versus metformin alone for mean difference with confidence intervals. The total mean difference is negative at -1.92 with a confidence interval of -4.43 to 0.59, indicating no statistically significant effect, and heterogeneity is high with an I-squared value of 100 percent.) /K 2 /P 8 0 R /Pg 33 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
